' Question: what does an Emergency Stop on the trading desk do to a running bot?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md. Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 06-emergency-stop
participant "EmergencyStopCommandHandler\n(trading)" as E
participant "bus" as BUS
participant BotEventRouter as RT
participant "GridFacts\n(bot's worker)" as F
participant "exchange" as X

E -> E : disable trading on the venue
E -> BUS : TradingSwitchChangedEvent\n(off, EMERGENCY_STOP)
BUS -> RT : on_switch
RT -> F : on_switch(False, EMERGENCY_STOP),\nfor each bot on the venue
F -> F : STARTING, RUNNING or PAUSED\n--switch_off--> HALTED
E -> X : cancel every open order
E -> X : close every position\n(Spot: sell above the session's baseline)
note over F : a later Resume re-plans the ladder;\na STOPPING bot waits instead
@enduml
